-- title:
--   At most h-n independent primitives modulo [p]_F
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, with $p$ prime, let $n$ be a natural number and let $F_0$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$, i.e. an $n$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ with zero constant term, linear part $X_i + Y_i$ and satisfying the associativity identity, assumed commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Write $[m]_{F_0}$ for the iterated series defined by $[0]_{F_0} = 0$ and $[m+1]_{F_0,i} = F_{0,i}([m]_{F_0}(X), X)$, let $I \subseteq k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ be the ideal generated by the $n$ components of $[p]_{F_0}$, and let $J \subseteq k[[X,Y]]$ be the ideal generated by the $2n$ series obtained from those components by substituting the first block $X$ and the second block $Y$ of variables. Assume that $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/I$ has $k$-dimension $p^h$ for a given natural number $h$. Then there are an $s \in \mathbb{N}$ with $s + n \le h$ and series $\psi_1,\dots,\psi_s \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ such that each $\psi_j$ has zero constant term and $\psi_j(F_0(X,Y)) - \psi_j(X) - \psi_j(Y) \in J$, and such that every $\psi'$ with zero constant term and $\psi'(F_0(X,Y)) - \psi'(X) - \psi'(Y) \in J$ satisfies $\psi' - \sum_{j} a_j \psi_j \in I$ for suitable scalars $a_j \in k$.
--
--   This is the statement that the homomorphisms from the $p$-torsion subgroup scheme $F_0[p]$ to the additive group, described concretely as power series that are primitive modulo $[p]_{F_0}$, span a $k$-space of dimension at most $h - n$, where $p^h$ is the order of $F_0[p]$; classically this is the inequality $\dim_k \mathrm{Hom}(F_0[p], \mathbb{G}_a) \le h - n$ coming from $\dim F + \dim F^{D} = \mathrm{ht}\,F$. It is used in the construction of rigidified symmetric two-cocycles for such a formal group law, via [`MvFormalGroup.exists_isSymmTwoCocycle_rigidified_span_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_isSymmTwoCocycle_rigidified_span_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow).
